A plain `.test { }` class is a static CSS rule — Tailwind's variant system (`md:`, `hover:`, etc.) only works on things it generates as utilities, so it can't prefix arbitrary custom classes. Use `@utility` instead:

```css
/* globals.css */
@utility test {
  background: red;
}
```
```html
<h3 className="md:test">text</h3>
```

Source: `src/docs/adding-custom-styles.mdx` (~line 406-437) — "Custom utilities" section: `@utility` registers the class into Tailwind's utilities layer, so it automatically works with variants like `hover`, `focus`, and `lg`/`md`.

